<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=skyscraper">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Building and engineering</p><h1 class="enc-title">Skyscraper</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1885">1885</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A skyscraper is a very tall building, typically defined as at least 150 metres high, of a type that first emerged in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in the late 19th century; many regard the ten-storey Home Insurance Building in Chicago, built in 1884–1885, as the first. Its architect, William Le Baron Jenney, made a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> frame carry the whole weight of the walls, and the building also used elevators, fireproofing and electrical wiring. Construction surged in the 1960s and boomed in East and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a> in the 1990s; over 7,000 now exceed 150 metres.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/skyscraper.jpg" alt="Skyscraper" width="320" height="531" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mark Ahsmann · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boerentoren_(cropped).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1885</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Chicago</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>William Le Baron Jenney · <a href="/empire/united-states">United States</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Which building came first is debated: some point to Philadelphia’s Jayne Building (1849–50) or New York’s Equitable Life Building (1870).</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/elevator">Safety elevator<span>1852</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/bessemer-process">Bessemer process<span>1856</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=skyscraper">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
